From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lance-linalg: add a portable riscv64 SIMD fallback (9.0.0)

lance-linalg's f32x8/f32x16/i32x8/f64x4/f64x8 SIMD types
(src/simd/{f32,f64,i32}.rs) are defined, and every trait impl for them
written, only under `#[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64"/"aarch64"/
"loongarch64")]`; riscv64 hits "cannot find type `f32x8` in this
scope" as soon as lance-linalg is built. Add an array-backed struct
plus a scalar implementation of every method the SIMD/FloatSimd traits
require, gated `#[cfg(not(any(target_arch = "x86_64", target_arch =
"aarch64", target_arch = "loongarch64")))]` beside the existing
per-architecture arms, which are otherwise untouched.

Same change as 0002/0004-lance-{core,linalg}-riscv64-simd-fallback.patch
(which target this crate's 7.0.0 release), rebased onto the 9.0.0
crates.io release that crates/lance-context-core's `lance = "9.0.0"`
pulls in; the fallback arms themselves are unchanged. Applied (via
0003-cargo-patch-lance-crates-for-riscv64.patch) to a local copy of
lance-linalg 9.0.0 materialized by the workflow, since it is a transitive
crates.io dependency and cannot be patched in place (CLAUDE.md gotcha
300).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to lance-format/lance]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
